  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Chlamydia Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result indicates that chlamydia was not detected in the sample. It suggests that the individual is not currently infected with Chlamydia trachomatis, the bacterium responsible for chlamydia infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result indicates the presence of Chlamydia trachomatis in the sample. It suggests that the individual is currently infected with chlamydia and requires appropriate treatment to clear the infection. Additionally, contact tracing and testing of sexual partners are essential to prevent further spread of the infection.</div></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p>",
